From ed2516e110eca8ac2fd9d589f43d6993944fbbe1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 08:06:47 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix: seed demo messages in the past and make broadcast
 failure non-fatal

Seeded messages used a fixed time of day (16:40), which is in the future when
seeded earlier in the day, so newly sent messages sorted before them and
appeared to vanish after a reload. Seed times are now relative to now.

Sending no longer returns 500 when Reverb is not running; the message is
already saved, so the broadcast error is reported instead of thrown.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013nAYnSuKh83gFwTMS3A7jm
---
 app/Services/MessageService.php     |  8 +++++++-
 database/seeders/DatabaseSeeder.php | 23 ++++++++++++-----------
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/Services/MessageService.php b/app/Services/MessageService.php
index 2c444e9..27992f2 100644
--- a/app/Services/MessageService.php
+++ b/app/Services/MessageService.php
@@ -47,7 +47,13 @@ public function send(User $user, Conversation $conversation, array $data): Messa
             return $message->load(['sender', 'replyTo', 'attachments']);
         });
 
-        broadcast(new MessageSent($message))->toOthers();
+        // The message is already saved; a realtime hiccup (e.g. Reverb not running)
+        // must not turn a successful send into a 500.
+        try {
+            broadcast(new MessageSent($message))->toOthers();
+        } catch (\Throwable $e) {
+            report($e);
+        }
 
         return $message;
     }
